REUSE AND ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

This demonstrator deliberately reuses proven patterns from three earlier HPC
repositories rather than reinventing them. What follows states exactly what was
taken from each, and in what form, so a reviewer can verify the claim.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HARMONY — https://github.com/hpcbg/harmony
   Licence: MIT. The reused modules ship their own LICENSE files,
            "Copyright (c) 2026 Kaloyan Yovchev".
   HARMONY is HPC's ARISE demonstrator.

ADAPTED CODE (derived work, substantially modified):

  wisepack_ws/src/wisepack_fiware/dds/generate_config.py
      Adapted from  ros2-xarm-pack-bottle/ros2_ws/src/fiware_bridge/dds/
                    generate_config.py
      Reused: the DDS-eligibility rules for scalar std_msgs, the
      ROS `/a/b` -> DDS `rt/a/b` naming rule, the reserved-`status`-leaf
      exclusion, the NGSI-LD id derivation, and the output document shape.
      These encode end-to-end-validated knowledge about what Orion-LD's DDS
      bridge actually accepts, which is why they were reused rather than
      re-derived.
      Changed: WISEPACK has no NGSI-v2 node backend to fall back to, so an
      unbridgeable topic is a hard error here instead of a warning.

  wisepack_ws/src/wisepack_fiware/dds/docker-compose.dds.yml
      Adapted from  .../fiware_bridge/dds/docker-compose.dds.yml
      (itself derived from the ARISE ros2_fiware_basic_app example).
      Reused: the `-wip dds -mongocOnly` invocation, host networking + host
      IPC, and the context_broker_config.json mount point.
      Changed: WISEPACK container names, an added MongoDB health check.

  scripts/measure_dds_fiware_latency.py
      Adapted from  scripts/measure_dds_fiware_latency.py
      Reused: the whole measurement method — the t0..t3 timestamp model, the
      correction that references FIWARE->ROS from PATCH *initiation* because
      Orion writes to DDS while still processing the PATCH, the percentile
      helpers and the report/artefact shape.
      Changed: WISEPACK topics and entities; the PRIMARY metric is the one-way
      ROS->FIWARE audit hop rather than the closed loop.

  wisepack_ws/src/wisepack_fiware/config/bridge_config.yaml
      Structure (fiware:/ros_to_fiware:/fiware_to_ros:) adapted from
      .../fiware_bridge/config/bridge_config.yaml so HARMONY's generator could
      be reused. All entities, topics and attributes are WISEPACK's.

  wisepack_ws/src/wisepack_fiware/wisepack_fiware/verify.py
      The `orion_classify` REAL / UNINITIALIZED / MISSING rule and the
      explanation of what "uninitialized" means are taken from HARMONY's
      validate_dds_native_demo.sh.

  perception/providers/fasterrcnn_bottle.py
  perception/calibration.py
  perception/camera.py
      Adapted from  ai-bottle-detector-fiware/pipeline.py and camera.py
                    (MIT, "Copyright (c) 2026 Kaloyan Yovchev").
      Reused: the Faster R-CNN construction for three classes and the
      checkpoint-loading convention; the 0.5 confidence threshold; the ArUco
      corner-marker detection, the ordered marker/coordinate correspondence and
      the homography onto the declared plane; the persistent marker cache; the
      (1, 1) sentinel for an uncalibrated frame; the bottle/cap association by
      mask coverage; the yaw derivation from the object->cap vector measured ON
      THE PLANE; the annotated-image rendering and its colours; and the
      threaded grab-newest-frame camera loop.
      These were reused rather than re-derived because they are validated
      against this hardware and these weights: WISEPACK's regression test
      (tests/test_perception_detector_regression.py) reproduces the original
      implementation's measurements from a saved frame to 0.01 mm and 0.01 deg.
      Changed: the code is restructured into a WISEPACK provider behind a
      generic perception-provider interface, reads WISEPACK's own configuration
      (no config.json is generated or read), reports calibration state
      explicitly instead of leaving it to be inferred, adds bounded camera
      error reporting, and emits domain-neutral ObservationBatch documents.

      IMPORTANT: this is ADAPTED code, not a runtime integration. The required
      implementation is included in WISEPACK and runs from this repository, in
      WISEPACK's own perception environment. A HARMONY checkout is NOT required
      at runtime and is never imported, executed or read from; the property is
      enforced by tests/test_perception_independence.py.

